          "event_type": "geopolitical",
          "net_loss_gbp_m": null,
          "loss_description": "The Russia/Ukraine Conflict has caused significant disruption to worldwide economies in 2022, both directly through the invasion and indirectly through sanctions being imposed on Russia by the UK, EU and US. A management margin of $36.8m net of reinsurance and reinstatement premiums has been made. Given the nature of the Russia/Ukraine Conflict, the ultimate losses relating to the event are subject to a high degree of uncertainty. In response, the Syndicate has booked prudent reserves reflecting our exposure.",
