          "page": 6,
          "confidence": 0.9
        }
      ],
      "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate experienced a significant gross claims reserve strengthening of $146.569 million (123.30% of opening gross reserves) in 2022. This adverse development was primarily driven by the booking of prudent reserves in response to the Russia/Ukraine Conflict, the impact of economic inflation on ultimate losses, and the ongoing social inflation risk within longer-tail claims. The syndicate also noted several other large loss events contributing to uncertainty in reserving. A management prudence margin is consistently applied over actuarial best estimates to minimize adverse run-off deviation.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "The Russia/Ukraine Conflict has caused significant disruption to worldwide economies in 2022, both directly through the invasion and indirectly through sanctions being imposed on Russia by the UK, EU and US. A management margin of $36.8m net of reinsurance and reinstatement premiums has been made. Given the nature of the Russia/Ukraine Conflict, the ultimate losses relating to the event are subject to a high degree of uncertainty. In response, the Syndicate has booked prudent reserves reflecting our exposure.",
        "Recently, there have been several loss events which, due to their ongoing nature and impact across multiple product lines, are exceptionally difficult to reserve for with inherently uncertain ultimate losses.",
        "In 2021, we retained the elevated status due to the social inflation risk within claims. This year, with the ongoing Russia/Ukraine Conflict and inflation across the U.S. and Europe reaching its highest level for many years, we have performed a detailed analysis on the impact of inflation rates to ultimate losses and reserve levels. However, there remains considerable uncertainty and we have therefore again shown the risk as trending upwards.",
        "Whilst our longer tail lines, such as casualty, remain a small proportion of the overall book, these lines, due to their very nature, are more difficult to reserve for and will, over time, increase the inherent risk within this principal risk.",
        "In arriving at the level of claims provisions a margin is applied over and above the actuarial best estimate so as to minimise any adverse run-off deviation."
      ],
